You might also consider using an alternative parameterisation to the dirichlet distribution
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirichlet_distribution#Related_distributions
By reparamerterising into a set of independent gammas you could use Nimble's default samplers and save yourself the effort of seeking an alternative sampler.

It would be nifty if Nimble could by default exploit this reparameterisation when required.

